    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] The aircraft was built in response to a need for a dive bomber and anti-submarine aircraft that could be launched both from land and from an aircraft carrier.\n[2] The Junkers Ju 87 or Stuka (from \"Sturzkampfflugzeug\", \"dive bomber\") was a German dive bomber and ground-attack aircraft.\n[3] The Heinkel He 50 was a German World War II-era dive bomber, originally designed for the Imperial Japanese Navy.\n[4] The Heinkel He 118 was a prototype German monoplane dive bomber design that lost out to the Junkers Ju 87 \"Stuka\" in the 1930s, and was never ordered by the \"Luftwaffe\"."
